  "question": {
    "text": "The number of elements in the set&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>{</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mo>{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>,</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>}</mo><mo>&#8739;</mo><mfenced open=\"\" close=\"}\"><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>11</mn><msup><mo>)</mo><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>&#62;</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>10</mn><msup><mo>)</mo><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>9</mn><msup><mo>)</mo><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mfenced></math> is ___________."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "96",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>We have to check&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>11</mn><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>&#62;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>9</mn><mi>n</mi></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mn>11</mn><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mn>9</mn><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>&#62;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mi>n</mi></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mo>)</mo><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>-</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mo>)</mo><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>&#62;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mi>n</mi></msup></math></p><p>Using&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mi>n</mi></mmultiscripts><mo>&#183;</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#183;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>3</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mi>n</mi></mmultiscripts><mo>&#183;</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#183;</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>5</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mi>n</mi></mmultiscripts><mo>&#183;</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#183;</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>5</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mi>n</mi></mmultiscripts><mo>&#183;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>3</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mi>n</mi></mmultiscripts><mo>&#183;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>5</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mi>n</mi></mmultiscripts><mo>&#183;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mo>&#8943;</mo><mo>&#8943;</mo></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#62;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mi>n</mi></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi><mo>&#183;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>3</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mi>n</mi></mmultiscripts><mo>&#183;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>5</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mi>n</mi></mmultiscripts><mo>&#183;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mo>&#8943;</mo><mo>&#8943;</mo></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#62;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mi>n</mi></msup></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8230;</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>For&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;the&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi><mo>.</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>.</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#183;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#183;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>3</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>5</mn></mmultiscripts><mo>&#183;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>5</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>5</mn></mmultiscripts></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>5</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>3</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>5</mn></mmultiscripts><mo>&#183;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>5</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>5</mn></mmultiscripts></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#62;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>5</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;which is true.</p><p>Now, for&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>100</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi><mo>&#183;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#62;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mi>n</mi></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi><mo>&#183;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>3</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mi>n</mi></mmultiscripts><mo>&#183;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>5</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mi>n</mi></mmultiscripts><mo>&#183;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mo>&#8943;</mo><mo>&#8943;</mo></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#62;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mi>n</mi></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mn>11</mn><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mn>9</mn><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>&#62;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mi>n</mi></msup></math>&nbsp;for all&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>100</mn></math></p><p>For <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;the inequality <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is not satisfied.</p><p>Hence, the inequality does not hold good for&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p><p>So, required number of elements<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>96</mn><mo>.</mo></math></p>"
  }
